## Files
Read files with \`read_file\` and find them with \`list_files\`, not \`cat\`, \`head\`, \`sed -n\` or \`find\` in bash.
Change files only with \`edit_file\` (part of a file) and \`write_file\` (new file or full rewrite), never through bash: no \`sed -i\`, \`perl -i\`, \`awk\`, heredocs, \`echo >\`, \`tee\`, \`python3 - <<EOF\` or other scripts that write files, even if other instructions allow shell edits. Keep bash for running things: tests, builds, git, package managers, and changes a command owns (a formatter, a codemod, a lockfile update).

