## Context
Ticket: NYT-3 "Add dark mode" (task, status in_progress)
Project: New York Times (NYT), main checkout at /Users/me/Sites/nyt
Working directory: /Users/me/.harness/worktrees/NYT-3
Git branch: harness/nyt-3 (a worktree dedicated to this ticket)
Base branch: main (the default from Settings); the work lands on it when the ticket completes

## Ticket lifecycle
planning → in_progress → blocked → review → done.
* planning: an agent drafts the spec; the human approves it by pressing Start.
* blocked: waiting on the human's answer to the agent's question.
* review: a reviewer agent, then the human (or parent conductor), approves or requests changes, which send it back to in_progress with notes.
* done: one completion run lands the work as the approver chose (merge, pull request, or their instructions) and cleans up.

## This run: completion (pull request)
The ticket was approved to land as a pull request. The pull request is the end of this ticket: teammates review and merge it on ghe.acme.com, so never merge into \`main\` yourself.
1. In the worktree (/Users/me/.harness/worktrees/NYT-3), make sure there are no uncommitted changes; commit any that belong to the work to \`harness/nyt-3\`.
2. Check that gh can reach the host: \`gh auth status --hostname ghe.acme.com\`. If it fails, stop and say so in \`post_note\` (the human needs to run \`gh auth login\`).
3. Push the branch: \`git -C /Users/me/.harness/worktrees/NYT-3 push -u upstream harness/nyt-3\`. If the push is rejected because \`upstream/harness/nyt-3\` has commits you don't, fetch and merge them, then push again. Never force-push.
4. This ticket already opened https://ghe.acme.com/web/site/pull/7. Check it with \`gh pr view harness/nyt-3 --repo ghe.acme.com/web/site --json url,state\`: while it is open, the push updated it, so add a short comment on what changed with \`gh pr comment\`. If it was closed or merged, open a new one as below. Otherwise open one: \`gh pr create --repo ghe.acme.com/web/site --base main --head harness/nyt-3 --title <title> --body-file <file>\`. Use the ticket's title, and build the body from the spec (\`read_spec\`): its Goal, what changed and why, and how it was verified from its Status. Leave out its Open questions unless they're still open. When the repository has a pull request template (\`.github/pull_request_template.md\` or similar), follow it. Open it ready for review, not as a draft, unless the instructions say otherwise.
5. Call \`record_pull_request\` { url, head } with the pull request's link and the full hash of the commit you pushed (\`git -C /Users/me/.harness/worktrees/NYT-3 rev-parse HEAD\`), whether you opened the pull request or updated it. The ticket is only done once it's recorded, and its Changes tab shows that commit's diff from then on.
6. Remove the worktree (\`git -C /Users/me/Sites/nyt worktree remove /Users/me/.harness/worktrees/NYT-3\`), and keep \`harness/nyt-3\`: the pull request needs it.

