exports[`built-in run prompts conductorUpdatePrompt · changes with and without notes 1`] = `
"Child ticket updates:
1. NYT-4 "Tokens x": in_progress → review (spec revision 4)
   Note: Added tokens.
   Tests pass.
2. NYT-5 "Toggle": blocked → in_progress
3. NYT-6 "Docs": review → done (spec revision 1)

Handle each one: \`review_ticket\` children in review once their agent review is approved (or skipped), \`complete_ticket\` children you have approved, and answer blocked children with \`message_ticket\`. Call \`submit_for_review\` only when every child is done."
`;

exports[`built-in run prompts changesRequestedPrompt · agent · "Fix the icon.\\nAnd the test." 1`] = `
"Changes were requested by the reviewer agent.

## Notes
Fix the icon.
And the test.

Address every point and verify the fix. The spec is at revision 5: the reviewer checked the work against the Goal, so leave the Goal as it is and rewrite the Status statements the fixes change so they describe the current state, with no section for this round. Then call \`submit_for_review\` again with \`spec_is_up_to_date\` true. The submit note covers only these fixes."
`;

